[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/568107479","html_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/1165#issuecomment-568107479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/1165","id":568107479,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2ODEwNzQ3OQ==","user":{"login":"chrislusf","id":1543151,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NDMxNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1543151?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf","html_url":"https://github.com/chrislusf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-12-20T22:14:52Z","updated_at":"2019-12-20T22:22:11Z","body":"A side question, sort of customer survey: why do you prefer SeaweedFS over s3?\r\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/568107479/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/568145526","html_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/1165#issuecomment-568145526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/1165","id":568145526,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2ODE0NTUyNg==","user":{"login":"dqsully","id":9079721,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzk3MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9079721?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully","html_url":"https://github.com/dqsully","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-12-21T02:47:59Z","updated_at":"2019-12-21T03:05:22Z","body":"In regards to your question about why SeaweedFS over S3:\r\n\r\nWe needed a shared filesystem with all of these features:\r\n* Highly Available\r\n* Scalable\r\n* High Performance\r\n* Mounts to a Linux filesystem\r\n* If self-hosted, can run in Kubernetes without being tied to a specific machine\r\n* Can efficiently calculate disk usage\r\n\r\nWe considered pretty much every option out there:\r\n* Amazon S3 (doesn't support Unix filesystem properties very well)\r\n* Amazon EFS (only easy to calculate usage of total drive, and is limited to 100 drives for a 4-zone VPC, we would have needed >900)\r\n* Rook CephFS (tied to specific machines, hard to manage)\r\n* Rook EdgeFS (couldn't get it working, hard to manage)\r\n* GlusterFS (also tied to specific machines)\r\n* NFS (could not figure out high availability)\r\n* Portworx (also tied to specific machines)\r\n\r\nAnd I think there were a couple others that I can't remember.\r\n\r\nWe didn't originally consider SeaweedFS even though I had come across it in my searches because there werent't any Helm charts for it, but in the end it proved to be the best solution for our needs:\r\n* Highly Available (using StatefulSets, headless Services, and some Helm templating)\r\n* Scalable (^ same things for different reasons)\r\n* High Performance (especially after adding AWS zone affinity for both Mounter <-> Filer and Filer <-> Redis)\r\n* Mounts to a Linux filesystem (using a DaemonSet to manage privileged containers for mounting)\r\n* Is not tied to specific machines (Volume, Master, and Filer servers can run as normal pods backed by EBS volumes, which Kubernetes moves and manages)\r\n* Can efficiently calculate disk usage (since we are using Redis for the Filer backend, we can write code to scan through the raw file metadata and quickly tally up usage numbers)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/568145526/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/568146658","html_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/1165#issuecomment-568146658","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/1165","id":568146658,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2ODE0NjY1OA==","user":{"login":"dqsully","id":9079721,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzk3MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9079721?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully","html_url":"https://github.com/dqsully","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dqsully/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-12-21T03:05:00Z","updated_at":"2019-12-21T03:05:00Z","body":"I also have a question about the values in `scaffold.go`. Do you want these options to be enabled or disabled by default? I committed them as enabled by default since it should only help performance, but the Go Redis library has them disabled by default, so I'll leave it up to you.\r\n\r\nAlso, I don't think I explained this very well, but by default the Redis client will only read and write to the master server for a given shard. The `readOnly` option allows the Redis client to read from a shard's slave servers as well as the master, but all writes will still go to the master. `routeByLatency` enables `readOnly` when true, and allows the Redis client to query and automatically use the closest Redis server for reads instead of picking a random one.\r\n\r\nIn our case, one of our processes needs to get file information as fast as possible in a synchronous manner, so even sub-millisecond latencies add up. Enabling `routeByLatency` decreased our overall process times by at least 10% in zones that didn't have the Redis master, and probably decreased our time interacting with SeaweedFS by 30% or more.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/568146658/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/568152770","html_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/1165#issuecomment-568152770","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/1165","id":568152770,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2ODE1Mjc3MA==","user":{"login":"chrislusf","id":1543151,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NDMxNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1543151?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf","html_url":"https://github.com/chrislusf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrislusf/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-12-21T05:00:21Z","updated_at":"2019-12-21T05:00:39Z","body":"Thanks for the detailed answer! It is eye-opening to get this detailed feedback! Thanks!\r\n\r\nI address the default value concern with 62b1a346ef33e0d4aa84a568e32a53550b75b590 , please help to check whether it makes sense.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/568152770/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/568156218","html_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/1165#issuecomment-568156218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/1165","id":568156218,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29t